I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access. Fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`, and sending the input's text in that URL would also leak untrusted data. Neither is granted, so the world imports only the inference interface. If operations wants them, the graph's `with` clause has to be widened first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

